### 4. lib/views/cli.html — WebSocket, VAD, interrupt (full rewrite in outputs)
# See cli_wave2.html in outputs. Summary of changes vs wave-1 cli.html:
#
#  REMOVED: CHAT_URL, POLL_URL constants
#  REMOVED: HTTP POST /chat + setInterval polling /poll (entire pattern)
#  REMOVED: Visual character-by-character streaming timer (setInterval 12ms)
#
#  ADDED: connectWs() — opens ws:// on load, reconnects with backoff
#  ADDED: ws.onmessage handler — chunk|done|error|session message types
#  ADDED: sendMessage() — WS primary path; HTTP POST fallback if WS not ready
#  ADDED: VAD silence timer (1200ms) — auto-sends accumulated interim on silence
#  ADDED: interruptIfSpeaking() — user speech cancels TTS, returns to idle
#  ADDED: clearTimeout(vadTimer) in recognition.onend + onerror
#  ADDED: connectWs() call at boot (before auto-listen timeout)
#
#  RESULT: latency drops ~300-600ms (no poll round-trip); conversation feels
#  natural on mobile; no more "stuck in thinking" if poll misses a response.

